# macOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
._*

# Archived and temporary artifacts
archive/
*.zip
*.tar.gz
tmp/

# Runtime: state files belong to each project, not to version control
.hello-dev/

# Development journal: this repo's change log is not portable config and must not be committed by adopting projects.
# The journal stays unpublished, with one exception: _RULES.md is the authoritative log-rules file that
# published documents link to by path (AGENTS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, SKILL.md, modules/...), so leaving it
# out of the repository breaks those links in every clone. The directory is therefore excluded by contents
# (`docs/progress_coding/*`) rather than as a whole -- a negation cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the whole-directory form would make the line below a no-op.
docs/progress_coding/*
!docs/progress_coding/_RULES.md

# Host project-level workspace data (session state, daily logs, local scratch).
# This directory also holds throwaway baselines that duplicate SKILL.md under the same
# `name: hello-dev`; tracking them creates false skill-detection candidates. Pack output
# already excludes this path in scripts/portable.js -- this keeps it out of the repository too.
.workbuddy/
